system.ontology:
[Ontology] kind — layer rule · its traits; then each trait, whose fields the assembly_* tools take
part — placements may name it as their layer · LABELED, SOURCED, MODELED, PARAMETRIC, COUNTED
placement — never a layer · LABELED, PLACED, JOINED
step — never a layer · LABELED, ASSEMBLED, INSTRUCTED, ANNOTATED, STAGED
guide — never a layer · LABELED, SEQUENCED, INSTRUCTED, ANNOTATED, STAGED
LABELED — A name and, optionally, a description. Example: { name: "Motor arm" }
SOURCED — Where a part's geometry came from — the back-pointer for the Blender round trip. Example: { file: "model.blend", object: "Frame_Bottom", scale: 0.05 }
MODELED — A part's own geometry as a file on the freight. A part that has only an interior carries none. Example: { file: "parts/arm.glb", tris: 80, bbox: [0.1263, 0.0075, 0.1729] }
PARAMETRIC — Geometry generated at read from a generator and its params. Example: { generator: "fastener.bolt", params: { thread: "M3", length: 16 } }
COUNTED — The kit's count of a part — what says it is a thing you order. Example: { qty: 6 }
PLACED — One occurrence of a part: which layer it is in, what it places, where. The same layer, parent and name again is an over — only what changes. Example: { layer: "motor", name: "propeller.0", ref: "propeller", translation: [0, 0.022, 0] }
JOINED — What a fastener's placement holds. Which kind of joint it is, is a joint.* symbol on the literal; how far it is done up is a step's note. Example: { joins: ["bottom_plate.0", "arm.0"] }
ASSEMBLED — What a step does to the build — the placements it names, by slug; the fold reads them in guide order. Example: { placements: [{ literal: "drone_rig.arm.0", active: true }] }
INSTRUCTED — What a step (or a guide's intro) tells the builder — numbered lines and media. Example: { lines: [{ text: "Thread the 16mm bolt." }], images: [] }
ANNOTATED — The callouts of a step or a guide. Example: { notes: [{ text: "Leave it loose.", symbols: ["note.warning", "warn.loose"] }] }
STAGED — How the stage shows a step or a guide's overview. Example: { camera: { target: [0, 0, 0], position: [0.3, 0.25, 0.3] }, explode: 0 }
SEQUENCED — A guide's subject and its steps in sections. Example: { subject: "drone_rig", sections: [{ name: "Frame", steps: ["drone.01", "drone.02"] }] }
